{
    "post_id": 69669,
    "title": "אֵימָתַי נִגְלָה לַנֶּאֱהָב | Eimatai Niglah la-Ne'ehav — an original 'Aqedah piyyuṭ by Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-10-29",
    "last_updated": "2026-10-29",
    "excerpt": "'Aqedah piyyuṭim are generally, in Ashkenazi seliḥot cycles, the second-to-last seliḥa, preceding the pizmon. Traditionally written in rhyming quatrains, they retell the narrative of the binding of Isaac. There are dozens of 'aqedah piyyutim, but almost all of them focus on the perspective of Abraham. This is unsurprising, since Abraham's perspective is largely the focus in the midrash. But it always felt like a bit of a lost opportunity to me. I've always sympathized more with Isaac's perspective, perhaps for obvious reasons (my Hebrew name is <span class=\"hebrew\">יצחק הראל בן אברהם הכהן</span> Isaac Mountain-of-God son of Abraham, the Person-who-sacrifices, after all). And the question of when did Isaac realize what was happening, and how did he react to it, is a fascinating and disturbing one to me. This 'aqedah is meant to reflect that question. Directed at Isaac, it asks him: when did you know, and how did you respond when you did? And will you remember us before God?",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\n&#8216;Aqedah piyyuṭim are generally, in Ashkenazi seliḥot cycles, the second-to-last seliḥah, preceding the pizmon. Traditionally written in rhyming quatrains, they retell the narrative of the binding of Isaac. There are dozens of &#8216;aqedah piyyutim, but almost all of them focus on the perspective of Abraham. This is unsurprising, since Abraham&#8217;s perspective is largely the focus in the midrash. But it always felt like a bit of a lost opportunity to me. I&#8217;ve always sympathized more with Isaac&#8217;s perspective, perhaps for obvious reasons (my Hebrew name is <span class=\"hebrew\">יצחק הראל בן אברהם הכהן</span> Isaac Mountain-of-God son of Abraham, the Person-who-sacrifices, after all). And the question of when did Isaac realize what was happening, and how did he react to it, is a fascinating and disturbing one to me. This &#8216;aqedah is meant to reflect that question. Directed at Isaac, it asks him: when did you know, and how did you respond when you did? And will you remember us before God?\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">אֵ</span>ימָתַי נִגְלָה לַנֶּאֱהָב<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בֵּ</span>ן יָחִיד יַקִּיר כְּזָהָב<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">גָּ</span>מוּל בְּמִשְׁתֶּה אַֽהַב<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">דַּ</span>רְכְּךָ לַעֲלוֹת בַּלַּהַב׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhen was it revealed to the beloved,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Isaac. Most of this poem is addressing Isaac directly.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthe only son, as precious as gold, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nweaned in a feast of love, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n“Your path is to go up in flame?” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">הֲ</span>יָדַֽעְתָּ בְּאֶֽרֶץ פְּלֶֽשֶׁת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וַ</span>יַּשְׁכֵּם בַּשֶּֽׁמֶשׁ הַמְּחֻדֶּֽשֶׁת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">זְ</span>קֵנְךָ הָרִאשׁוֹן מִשְּׁלֹֽשֶׁת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">חָ</span>לַם חֲלוֹם לַעֲשׂוֹת מִצְוַת בֹּֽשֶׁת׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nDid you know in the land of Philistia, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nwhen he<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Abraham. For most of this poem, the second person is Isaac, and the third person is Abraham.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> woke up early in the renewed sun — <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nyour elder, first of three, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ndreamed a dream<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> According to the Rambam, Guide III 24:10, Abraham’s commandment to slaughter his son was received in a dream. Later commentators emphasized the fact that Abraham woke up early in the morning to do it.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> to do a shameful commandment? <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">טִ</span>יַּֽלְתָּ אִתּוֹ שְׁלֹֽשֶׁת יָמִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יָ</span>דַֽעְתָּ אֵין־שֶׂה לַפֶּחָמִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>י שָׁאַלְתָּ אַיֵּה שֶׂה בְּלִי־מוּמִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">לְ</span>הָבִין אִם־יַעַדְךָ שְׁפִיכַת דָּמִים׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nYou walked with him three days; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nyou knew there was no lamb for the coals. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nAs you asked, “Where is the unblemished lamb?” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nto understand if your destination was bloodshed. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">מָ</span>תַי הֵבַֽנְתָּ אֶת־תְּשׁוּבָתוֹ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נָ</span>א־הָבֵן הַבֵּן הַשֶּׂה אוֹתוֹ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">סִ</span>דֵּר עֲצֵי לֶהָבָתוֹ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">עֵ</span>ת בָּאָה אֵין־סָפֵק שֶׁיְּדַעְתּוֹ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhen did you understand his answer? <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nUnderstand, the son is the very lamb! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nHe arranged the wood of his fire; <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\na time came, doubtlessly you knew it. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">פֵּ</span>רְשׁוּ הַחֲכָמִים כִּי קִבַּֽלְתָּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צַ</span>ו לָצָו קַו לָקָו לֹא בָּהַֽלְתָּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">קָ</span>רָֽאתָ לְמִמֶּֽנּוּ גֻּדַּֽלְתָּ<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">רַ</span>ק זְכוּתִי שֶׁאוֹתִי כָּבַֽלְתָּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe sages interpreted that you accepted: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ncommand to command, rule to rule,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Isaiah 28:10&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> you did not panic. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nYou called to the one from whom you were raised, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n“It is only my merit that I be tied up. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שְׁ</span>מֹר לִשְׁחֹטִי כַּהֲלָכָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">תָּ</span>בִיא לְאִמִּי יִסְכָּה<br />\nאֶת־עֲפָרַי הָרְאוּיִים לַלִּשְׁכָּה<br />\nנָא אַל־תִּתְמַהְמֵֽהַּ לֶךְ־לְךָ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nKeep my slaughter as per the law!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Genesis Rabbah 56:8&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBring to my mother Yiscah<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> According to the midrash, Sarah. See Sifrei Bamidbar 99:1 and Megillah 14a.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nmy ashes,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Sefer haYashar, Vayera 20&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> worthy of the chamber;<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Referring, by synecdoche, to the Temple&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nplease do not delay, go forth!”\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nיָדַעְתָּ לְפִי הַמִּדְרָשִׁים<br />\nיַׄעַדְךָ לְהַעֲלוֹת בְּאִשִּׁים<br />\nצָׄרִיךְ אֲנִי לְחַדֵּשׁ חִדּוּשִׁים<br />\nחׇׄכְמָה הִיא אֵינָהּ בִּכְתַב הַחֻמָּשִׁים׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nYou knew, according to the midrashim,<br />\nyour destination was to go up in flame.<br />\nI must bring a new novelty:<br />\nthis wisdom is not in the written Pentateuch!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[9]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Nowhere in the written Torah does it state that Isaac knew what was happening.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nקׇׄרְבָּן אַף־עַל־פִּי שֶׁלֹּא־נִפְטַֽרְתָּ<br />\nהָׄיִֽיתָ כְּׄאִֽלּוּ הֻבְעַֽרְתָּ<br />\nהֲׄלֹא נֶׄאֱמַר שֶׁאֵלָיו לֹא־דִּבַּֽרְתָּ<br />\nבֵּׄיןׄ אַׄבְׄרָׄהָׄםׄ וּבֵינְךָ הִתְפַּזַּֽרְתָּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nA sacrifice, though you did not pass on,<br />\nyou were, as if you were burned.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[10]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Midrash Tanchuma, Vayera 23:8&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nIs it not said that you did not speak to him?<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[11]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> After the Akedah, Abraham and Isaac are never in the same location again. The next time Isaac sees his father it is his corpse. There is total separation between the two.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nBetween Abraham and you, you were scattered!\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nחֹׄק הוּא לְזַרְעֲךָ הַנּוֹשֵׂא<br />\nזִׄכְרוֹן הַשּׁוֹחֵט וְהַשֶּׂה<br />\nקָׄרֵב שִׁירֵֽינוּ כֶּעָשָׁן הַמִּתְנַשֵּׂא<br />\nלָאֵל מֶֽלֶךְ יוֹשֵׁב עַל־כִּסֵּא׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nIt is a law for your seed, bearing<br />\nthe memory of the slaughterer and the lamb.<br />\nBring near our song, like ascending smoke,<br />\nto the Sovereign Deity sitting on the throne!<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_12');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[12]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> A formulaic conclusion for an ‘aqedah poem, designed to lead into a recitation of the Thirteen Attributes.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_12', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Isaac. Most of this poem is addressing Isaac directly.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Abraham. For most of this poem, the second person is Isaac, and the third person is Abraham.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >3</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">According to the Rambam, Guide III 24:10, Abraham’s commandment to slaughter his son was received in a dream. Later commentators emphasized the fact that Abraham woke up early in the morning to do it.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >4</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">See Isaiah 28:10</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >5</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Genesis Rabbah 56:8</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >6</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">According to the midrash, Sarah. See Sifrei Bamidbar 99:1 and Megillah 14a.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >7</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">See Sefer haYashar, Vayera 20</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >8</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Referring, by synecdoche, to the Temple</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >9</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Nowhere in the written Torah does it state that Isaac knew what was happening.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >10</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Midrash Tanchuma, Vayera 23:8</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >11</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">After the Akedah, Abraham and Isaac are never in the same location again. The next time Isaac sees his father it is his corpse. There is total separation between the two.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_12\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_12');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >12</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">A formulaic conclusion for an ‘aqedah poem, designed to lead into a recitation of the Thirteen Attributes.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').hide(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('+'); } function footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1() { if (jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').is(':hidden')) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); } else { footnote_collapse_reference_container__1(); } } function footnote_moveToReference__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } } function footnote_moveToAnchor__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } }</script>",
